Subject: H2, Ed25519 signature length on the sodium path
Reason: On PHP below 8.4 EdDSA is verified with sodium, which throws SodiumException (not WebAuthnException) for a signature that is not 64 bytes (audit 3); such a signature now simply fails to verify.

diff -ruN a/WebAuthn.php b/WebAuthn.php
--- a/WebAuthn.php
+++ b/WebAuthn.php
@@ -519,6 +519,11 @@
                 if ($rawPk && \strlen($rawPk) === 44 && \substr($rawPk,0, \strlen($okpPrefix)) === $okpPrefix) {
                     $publicKeyXCurve = \substr($rawPk, \strlen($okpPrefix));
 
+                    // sodium throws SodiumException for a signature that is not 64 bytes.
+                    if (!\is_string($signature) || \strlen($signature) !== 64) {
+                        return false;
+                    }
+
                     return \sodium_crypto_sign_verify_detached($signature, $dataToVerify, $publicKeyXCurve);
                 }
             }
